"assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hi MAVSDK team,\n\nI am currently working with an omnicopter (a fully actuated 6-DoF vehicle). I need to control its lateral translation (moving along the X and Y axes) while keeping the drone perfectly level (Pitch and Roll at 0).\n\nCurrently, Offboard::set_attitude() only accepts a scalar thrust value, which seems to only apply to the Z-axis.\n\nIs there any existing interface, workaround, or planned feature in MAVSDK that allows sending a 3D thrust vector (X, Y, Z thrust) to PX4 to control an omnicopter?\n\nThank you!", "closed_by": {"login": "yygbruce", "id": 18020338, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDIwMzM4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18020338?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce", "html_url": "https://github.com/yygbruce", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yygbruce/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2897/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2897/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null}, "comments": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/4686670833", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2897#issuecomment-4686670833", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2897", "id": 4686670833, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s8AAAABF1jr8Q", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-06-12T02:03:14Z", "updated_at": "2026-06-12T02:03:14Z", "body": "I think the [MANUAL_CONTROL message]() can do it in theory, right?\n\nThat being said, I'm not sure it's a broadly required feature that needs adding to the MAVSDK API, as that one is supposed to be a subset of MAVLink covering a broad percentage of use.\n\nHave you considered using MavlinkDirect to send that message? ", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.c